node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Everything generated from the spec checkout, and nothing else, lives here:
# the JSON-LD data written by scripts/build-spec-data.mjs, and the TypeScript
# tables scripts/build-record-types.mjs and scripts/build-terms.mjs derive from
# it under src/spec/derived/.
#
# One directory, one rule, no exceptions. Not committed on purpose: a generated
# artifact cannot fall behind its source, because there is no copy to go stale.
# CI clones the commit conformance/scripts/SPEC_PIN names and points
# CASCADE_SPEC_DIR at it, so every CI build uses pinned data with nobody having
# to remember anything. The cost is that npm run build needs a spec checkout,
# exactly as npm test already does — and pretest and pretypecheck run
# npm run generate, so a clean clone builds what it needs before it needs it.
src/spec/

# Editor config: share what describes the project, keep what describes a person.
# Denying the directory first means a settings.json or a credentials file dropped
# here later is ignored by default rather than riding along in someone's commit.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
